                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[b][i]Switch 'N' Shoot[/i] is an outstanding single-button arcade shooter.[/b] This is the kind of games that pizza joints dream of. If I were pumping in quarters, I'd be flat broke. It is utterly addicting and just really really fun.\n\n[b]Some say this is the [i]Downwell[/i] of 2016, and I totally agree.[/b] It has that simple-yet-crazy-addictive mechanic that just keeps you saying 'one more run!'.\n\n[i]Essentially, every time you press a button (ie. space bar or mouse click), you shoot BUT you also change direction.[/i] You collect coin-like objects that upgrade your gun, and if you upgrade enough you move to the next level. This increases your score multiplier when you inevitably die.\n\n[b]Pros:[/b]\n+Outstanding novel game mechanic that is utterly addictive\n+Price is too cheap\n+Leaderboards are tons of fun for games like this\n+I like the ability to swap colors for everything in game\n\n[b]Cons:[/b]\n-I want more=D\n-It would be cool to have different artwork appear on the side panels\n-I think they should add more ships and colors and weapons and levels!\n\n[b]Totally worth two bucks.[/b] The trailer doesn't cut it, you have to play this to feel the addictiveness.",
